https://flapjax.surge.sh/skill.md . These are first-party PURPOSE assertions, not on-chain proof that work was actually performed.\n\nRPC evidence used: https://bsc-dataseed.binance.org ; fallback https://bsc-dataseed1.defibit.io ; https://bsc-rpc.publicnode.com for finalized/block-hash checks. Raw request/response records are in `rpc_evidence.jsonl`. Binance/Defibit rejected historical log queries even after shrinking; PublicNode required a personal archive token; dRPC returned range/rate errors; llama endpoint failed DNS. The shared p1.json was HTML, not JSON. The initial pin was superseded due missing-trie-node state pruning. All final balance/code reads and pool identity reads finished in 14.35 seconds after a fresh finalized pin. This is disclosed rather than silently substituting latest for historical calls.\n\n### Counting and classification assumptions\n- Holder means every address with balanceOf > 0, including contracts, dust, and the dead burn sink; shares use totalSupply, not ex-burn supply.\n- Holder candidates come from all three BscScan holder-index pages plus every receipt-verified treasury counterparty (the index omitted one positive payee); all 260 candidates were balance/code checked at the final pin and 255 positive balances sum exactly to totalSupply.\n- We did NOT complete an all-history token Transfer replay: archive/log RPC attempts failed.\n- The first draft pin was superseded because free RPC state was pruned; final state reads finished in 14.35 seconds after repinning finalized.\n- Primary Relay cohort follows the user operational definition, all treasury outflows in UTC [2026-10-12,2026-10-18); actual purpose is ambiguous.\n- Supplemental Q21-Q32 cohort is first-party label based, not inferred from token amounts.\n- Out-only-bounty MATCH is CONDITIONAL: 212 outflows have public project work/reward labels; six direct wallet transfers lack a captured label and are assumed payouts rather than sales.\n- This is not independent proof of the purpose or quality of every bounty.\n- No observed treasury outflow entered either pool, a router, or an unlabelled deployed contract; all 218 were treasury-signed calls directly to the token.\n- Never-sold MATCH is scoped to this ledger and attributable direct movements, not undisclosed common ownership of recipients.\n- Empty code is a code-status test, not proof of key ownership; delegated EIP-7702 EOAs are called out separately.\n- Retention balance>=payout does not prove coins were never moved/replenished.\n- Outflow scanning was receipt-verified for the five failed broad-cohort wallets only; other outflow flags are unknown, not false.\n- Public nodes prune history: subsequent historic eth_call requires a state-serving/archive node; BscScan and raw receipts provide independent public checks.\n- Confidence is a qualitative assessment, not a statistical probability.\n\n## Top ten (exact balances; total-supply shares)\n| Rank | Address | FLAPJAX | % total supply | Code/type |\n|---:|---|---:|---:|---|\n| 1 | `0xca93ec685b8623688e6b236f9068034b298c2150` | 20131436370.267389168985465000 | 45.295731833555% | PancakeSwap V3 FLAPJAX/WBNB 1% pool; token0/token1/fee/factory/getPool verified at pin. |\n| 2 | `0x740a3b4a91cb8fa47e85d7f9713ca6ec2f8a037e` | 5619844348.598993998769163970 | 12.644649784474% | PancakeSwap V3 BTCB/FLAPJAX 1% pool; factory identity verified at pin. |\n| 3 | `0x58fab046ce77064bf52c2eff4e163eb84386b8b4` | 2334009348.875000000000000000 | 5.251521035021% | Empty-code wallet at pinned block; ownership/control not inferred. |\n| 4 | `0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dead` | 1923471159.703770945293578174 | 4.327810109377% | Burn sink; empty code, not a spendable plain wallet. |\n| 5 | `0x2ea90ff709b0fb5decd1de944f644eecdc26d33a` | 1175621343.198940751591630110 | 2.645148022224% | Empty-code wallet; BscScan Flapjax Deployer label and initial treasury seed sender. |\n| 6 | `0x8e3dc66bb96b063afb932660fb5d060e170cf2cd` | 747196241.459736162058309614 | 1.6